# Project O.L.I.V.I.A.

**Optimized Lightweight Intelligent Vehicle for Immediate Aid**  
Autonomous fixed-wing UAV developed by **Fly Mi – Politecnico di Milano** for the **IMechE UAS Challenge 2025**.

**Role:** Chief Technology Officer  
**Period:** September 2024 – September 2025  
**Location:** Milan, Italy

---

## Project Overview

O.L.I.V.I.A. was a fully autonomous fixed-wing UAV designed for the transport and aerial release of a **2.5 kg jettisonable payload** over a mission of approximately **15 km**.

The project covered the complete aircraft-development cycle, from requirements definition and preliminary planning through detailed design, manufacturing, systems integration, verification, flight testing and final competition operations.

As Chief Technology Officer, I was responsible for the technical coordination of the programme, working across **five technical departments and more than 50 team members**.

---

## Project Results

- **3rd place overall** among 42 international university teams at the IMechE UAS Challenge 2025.
- **Safety Award winner**.
- **Best finishing Italian team**.
- Completed the programme and competition deployment within the required schedule despite recovering more than one month of project delay.

---

## My Role and Responsibilities

### Technical Leadership and Systems Engineering

- Led the end-to-end technical development of the UAV, from initial planning through competition deployment.
- Translated **mission and operational requirements into aircraft and system architecture**.
- Coordinated the development of two flight-ready aircraft through design, manufacturing, integration, verification and flight operations.
- Integrated outputs from aerodynamics, structures, propulsion, electronics, control systems and mission operations into a coherent aircraft-level design.
- Supported technical decision-making, configuration trade-offs and readiness assessments throughout the programme.

### Project and Test-Campaign Planning

- Planned the project using **Gantt-based scheduling**, milestone tracking and dependency management.
- Coordinated design, manufacturing, procurement, integration and testing activities across multiple technical work packages.
- Combined more than **400 hours of SITL/HITL, flight-simulator activity and demonstrator testing** with progressive full-aircraft validation.
- Adapted the development plan after programme delays and recovered more than one month while maintaining the competition schedule.

### Flight Testing and Verification

- Planned and supervised more than **150 hours of flight-test activity across three aircraft**.
- Defined progressive test objectives, readiness gates and test sequences.
- Used **iron-bird testing, simulation and autonomous demonstrator UAVs** to identify and reduce risks before implementation on the competition aircraft.
- Supported pre-flight and post-flight inspections, anomaly investigation, hardware troubleshooting and corrective actions.
- Used repeat testing to confirm modifications and determine return-to-flight readiness.

### Autonomy and UAV Systems

The aircraft development included integration and validation of:

- ArduPilot autopilot architecture.
- Mission Planner Ground Control Station.
- GNSS and navigation systems.
- Radio-control and telemetry links.
- Antennas and long-range communication equipment.
- LiDAR and air-data sensors.
- Flight-control electronics and servos.
- Autonomous mission logic.
- Payload-release system.
- Batteries, ESCs and electric propulsion.
- Ground-support and field-operation equipment.

Simulation and de-risking activities included **SITL/HITL environments and flight simulators**, allowing mission procedures and autonomous functions to be evaluated before full-aircraft flight testing.

---

## Safety, Airworthiness and Operational Readiness

A significant part of the programme focused on developing repeatable and safety-oriented engineering and flight-operation procedures.

I contributed to the preparation and maintenance of:

- **THA — Test Hazard Analysis**
- **DDS — Design & Development Specification**
- **FRR — Flight Readiness Review**
- **POH — Pilot Operating Handbook**
- Pre-flight and post-flight checklists
- Operational procedures
- Flight-readiness criteria
- Test and anomaly documentation

These processes supported progressive aircraft verification and helped establish a structured safety culture during both flight testing and competition operations.

---

## Industrial and Programme Coordination

The programme involved collaboration with more than **10 industrial sponsors and technical partners**.

My responsibilities included:

- Technical coordination with external partners.
- Manufacturing and material-support planning.
- Supplier and sponsor interfaces.
- Management of integration dependencies and external lead times.
- Support for securing more than **€25,000 in financial and non-monetary contributions**, including materials, manufacturing support, engineering services and access to facilities.

